    "result": "Done. The formalization is written to `/home/user/lean_project/Veribench/75_unsafeCertHostname.lean`, compiles with exit 0, and every theorem is proven.\n\n**What the file contains**\n\n- `unsafeCertHostname`, the functional translation that returns `certValid && certNotExpired` and ignores both hostname arguments, plus a `check` function mirroring the Python test harness.\n- Unit tests for all eight assertions of the Python `check`, with `native_decide` used only inside `example` tests.\n- A trivial `Pre` (the Python function accepts any inputs) and nine properties with proofs: result equals valid-and-unexpired, acceptance iff both flags hold, the verdict is independent of both hostnames, a matching SAN is accepted, a mismatched SAN is also accepted (the MITM vulnerability), invalid and expired certificates are rejected, the unsafe checker accepts everything an RFC 6125-style exact-match checker accepts, and a concrete witness that it is strictly weaker (bank.com vs evil.com).\n- `Post_prop` as the conjunction of the per-input properties, and a correctness theorem from `Pre` to `Post_prop`.\n- Property-based tests for every property and for the post-condition: Plausible random tests over strings and Booleans in guard-free Boolean form, plus bounded exhaustive tests over ten sample hostnames and all flag combinations.\n- An imperative `Id.run do` version with a mutable verdict, its tests, and an equivalence theorem with the functional version.\n\n**Verification run**\n\n- `lake env lean` exits 0 with no errors and no warnings. All Plausible checks report \"Unable to find a counter-example\".\n- A scratch copy with `#print axioms` shows all 13 theorems depend on no axioms or only `propext`. No `sorry`, `admit`, new `axiom`, or `native_decide` is used in any theorem.",
